Floor-pin `huggingface_hub` so a rebuild cannot re-resolve into the Xet
gated-repo download bug.

huggingface_hub PR #4394 (v1.2x) added a tree-listing cache that skips the
per-file HEAD call for Xet files and rebuilds the file metadata from the cached
/tree API response. On GATED repos the Hub returns a REDACTED xetHash
placeholder (64 `*`) there, which hub handed straight to hf_xet:

  RuntimeError: Task error: Unable to parse string as hex hash value

Every fresh `snapshot_download` of a gated model died on it (hf_preload Job,
the sglang/vllm shard Jobs, the pod model-download initContainers), while
`hf_hub_download` was fine because it goes through HEAD. hf_xet was never at
fault. Fixed by huggingface_hub PR #4595 ("[Download] Reject redacted Xet
hashes from tree cache", merged 2026-07-28, closes xet-core#895), released in
huggingface_hub v1.26.0 on 2026-07-30. Full history: FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md.

Neither `huggingface_hub` nor `hf_xet` is pinned anywhere in the build (the
scitrera Dockerfile installs whatever the sglang/transformers/flashinfer
resolve pulls in), so the fixed version is in the image only by accident of
build date. That is fine while the cluster still ships the
`HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1` workaround (repo var `hf_hub_disable_xet`), but the
moment that is flipped back to 0 an unlucky re-resolve would silently
reintroduce the crash. This adds the floor as a build knob:

  ARG HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=""   # empty = leave hub alone (all older recipes)
  HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0   # in sglang-0.5.16-sm121.recipe and later

Mechanism mirrors dockerfile-kernels-pin.patch / dockerfile-accelerate.patch:
an `ARG` + gated `uv pip install` RUN in the builder stage, before the
dist-packages split, so it is carried into the runtime stage.

PLACEMENT: this block goes LAST in the builder stage, immediately before the
`# Break up dist-packages ...` split, i.e. AFTER the `uv pip install ./python`
sglang step and after the DSV4 FlashMLA block. A floor installed earlier could
be undone by any later resolve. The hunk is TRAILING-CONTEXT-ONLY (anchored on
the upstream split block), so it applies regardless of which optional
dockerfile-*.patch steps ran before it, and it must therefore be applied LAST
in apply_patches().

It is a FLOOR (>=), not an exact pin: hub is not in the inference hot path and
no upper bound is known to be needed. Turn it into `==` here if a future hub
release ever regresses. Deliberately installed WITH deps, since a floor bump
may require a newer filelock/fsspec that `--no-deps` would leave unsatisfied.

Remove when the sglang base image itself carries a hub >= 1.26.0 floor.

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly in the local clone of
scitrera/cuda-containers.

--- a/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
+++ b/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
@@ -469,3 +469,24 @@
+# dgxarley: floor-pin huggingface_hub. Hub's tree-listing cache (PR #4394) fed
+# the redacted xetHash placeholder that the Hub /tree API returns for GATED
+# repos straight into hf_xet, which rejected it with "Unable to parse string as
+# hex hash value", killing every fresh snapshot_download of a gated model
+# (hf_preload Job, shard Jobs, the pod model-download initContainers). Fixed by
+# huggingface_hub PR #4595, released in v1.26.0 (2026-07-30); hf_xet itself was
+# never at fault. Nothing in this image pins hub, so without a floor a rebuild
+# can re-resolve back into the broken 1.2x window and silently re-break Xet
+# downloads once HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1 is dropped. Placed LAST in the builder
+# stage, after the sglang install, so no earlier step can downgrade it. Gated by
+# HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION (empty = leave hub alone, so every older recipe is
+# unaffected). Deliberately WITH deps: a floor bump may need a newer filelock or
+# fsspec, and --no-deps would leave that unsatisfied. See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md.
+ARG HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=""
+RUN --mount=type=cache,id=uv-cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
+    if [ -n "$HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION" ]; then \
+        echo "=== Enforcing huggingface_hub>=${HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION} (xet gated-repo fix) ==="; \
+        uv pip install "huggingface_hub>=${HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION}"; \
+        python3 -c "import huggingface_hub as h; print('huggingface_hub', h.__version__)"; \
+    fi
+
 # Break up dist-packages into smaller layers to avoid hitting Docker layer size limits
 COPY stages/directory_split2.sh /opt/directory_split2.sh
 RUN chmod +x /opt/directory_split2.sh && \
